#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 15394..16648
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/12
msgid ""
"How about this: I will give you a thorough\n"
"education,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 35876..13513
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/13
msgid ""
"Mr. First-Time Ornithologist.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/14
msgid ""
"Uh, OK. Start by telling me about the quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/0
msgid ""
"Cécile, what's that machine you said you use to\n"
"make those recordings of yours?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/1
msgid ""
"A cassette... something or other.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/2
msgid ""
"A cassette recorder? Or a cassette densuke, as\n"
"they say in Japon.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/3
msgid ""
"Yeah, that. What is that thing, anyway?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/4
msgid ""
"A portable recording device released last year by a\n"
"Japanese company: Sony.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/5
msgid ""
"It uses compact cassettes, making it far lighter\n"
"than open reel machines.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/6
msgid ""
"It still weighs 5 kilograms, but the exercise won't\n"
"kill me!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/7
msgid ""
"Ha.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/8
msgid ""
"It's user-friendly, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/9
msgid ""
"All the buttons have markings on them,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/10
msgid ""
"allowing you to operate it without looking at it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/11
msgid ""
"Can you imagine missing the shot of a lifetime\n"
"simply because you'd blinked?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/12
msgid ""
"That would be devastating.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/13
msgid ""
"But where'd they come up with densuke? It sounds\n"
"like a Japanese name.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/14
msgid ""
"Allow me to field that one.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/15
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/6
msgid ""
"Kaz?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/16
msgid ""
"Densuke's a nickname that comes from the name\n"
"of an old manga character.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/17
msgid ""
"Was he some recording nerd, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/18
msgid ""
"Don't gimme that! Recording atmospheric noises is\n"
"an exhilarating art!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/19
msgid ""
"There's nothing like capturing the real world in\n"
"action on tape!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/20
msgid ""
"It's just like taking pictures with a camera,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/21
msgid ""
"only with a microphone instead of a viewfinder.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/22
msgid ""
"Sure...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/23
msgid ""
"Listen to a tape with your eyes closed\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/24
msgid ""
"and the scene just bursts to life in your mind's eye.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/25
msgid ""
"Tell him, Cécile.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/26
msgid ""
"Absolutely. When I listen to the sounds of birds in\n"
"my apartment,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/27
msgid ""
"it's like I'm back in the forest where I recorded\n"
"them.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/28
msgid ""
"See, she's a Parisienne. She knows what's chic.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/29
msgid ""
"If you say so...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/30
msgid ""
"What do you like to record, Monsieur Miller?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/31
msgid ""
"Me? Steam locomotives, no question.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/32
msgid ""
"The roar of the engine, the throaty steam whistle...\n"
"More animal than machine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/33
msgid ""
"Mmh, don't get me started!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/34
msgid ""
"Steam locomotives are a dying breed in Japan.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/35
msgid ""
"I wouldn't mind going back for a bit and making\n"
"some new tapes while I still can.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/36
msgid ""
"...You're less civilized than I thought.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/37
msgid ""
"L-LESS civilized?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/38
msgid ""
"I detest those beasts. The noise frightens off all\n"
"the birds.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/39
msgid ""
"Then there's the smoke...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/40
msgid ""
"I much prefer the peace and quiet of the forest.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/41
msgid ""
"Cécile, wait! That... That came out wrong, I...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/42
msgid ""
"Sure it did.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/0
msgid ""
"You said you could do a monkey call.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/1
msgid ""
"Yes! Want to hear it?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, I won't be able to get it off my mind until I do.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/3
msgid ""
"Alright. Here it is, then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/4
msgid ""
"...That's pretty good.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/5
msgid ""
"I can do others, too. Like a sheep, a pig...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/6
#: codec/1/238/0xee440/19
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/17
msgid ""
"Yeah?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/7
msgid ""
"Wow. What about a pig?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/8
msgid ""
"That's uncanny!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/9
msgid ""
"Ha ha. I can do a rabbit as well.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/10
msgid ""
"A rabbit? Rabbits make noises?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/11
msgid ""
"Certainly. But they're very faint,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/12
msgid ""
"so perhaps only someone who has owned one\n"
"would recognize them.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/13
msgid ""
"I see. So what do they sound like?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/14
msgid ""
"Listen very carefully.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/16
msgid ""
"Seriously? Rabbits sound like that?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/17
msgid ""
"I assure you, they do. Listen again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/18
msgid ""
"Never heard a rabbit do that before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/19
msgid ""
"They do, I swear!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is the home to many hummingbirds as\n"
"well.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/1
msgid ""
"The people here call them colibri.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/2
msgid ""
"Colibri, huh...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/3
msgid ""
"Hummingbirds are the world's smallest birds.\n"
"Although they can vary from species to species,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/4
msgid ""
"most are around 10 cm in length, and the smallest\n"
"no more than five.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/5
msgid ""
"It's amazing to think that something so small can\n"
"still be a fully developed bird.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/6
msgid ""
"I'd think a bird that tiny would get mistaken for a\n"
"bug.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/7
msgid ""
"Actually they are often mistaken for sphinx moths.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/8
msgid ""
"The little darlings feed on flower nectar,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/9
msgid ""
"and their beaks are long and thin to help them\n"
"drink up the nectar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/10
msgid ""
"They beat their wings far faster than any other\n"
"bird.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/11
msgid ""
"The smallest ones over 70 times a second! Can\n"
"you imagine?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/12
#: codec/1/265/0x109080/13
msgid ""
"What for?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/13
msgid ""
"They hover in midair while they suck their nectar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/14
msgid ""
"They can even fly straight backwards.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/15
msgid ""
"Hovering... like a helicopter!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/16
msgid ""
"That's why Amanda and her unit called that\n"
"chopper colibri.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/17
msgid ""
"I think it is an insult to the birds to give their\n"
"names to weapons, don't you?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/18
msgid ""
"Don't ask me. Ask the birds how they feel about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/0
msgid ""
"Have you heard of the manakins?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/1
msgid ""
"Never.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/2
msgid ""
"Unbelievable! You came all the way to Costa Rica\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/3
msgid ""
"and you've never even heard of them!?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/4
msgid ""
"I didn't come here to look at...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/5
msgid ""
"Manakins are known for their beautiful courtship\n"
"dances.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/6
msgid ""
"The Orange-collared Manakin is said to live on the\n"
"Pacific side,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/7
msgid ""
"the White-bearded Manakin on the Caribbean side,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/8
msgid ""
"and the Long-tailed Manakin is in the central basin.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/9
msgid ""
"The Long-tailed Manakins are especially distinctive.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/10
msgid ""
"What's special about them?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/11
msgid ""
"First, each young male picks an older male to\n"
"teach him how to dance.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/12
msgid ""
"Then teachers and pupils all get in a group and\n"
"dance for the females.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/13
msgid ""
"However, only the teachers get paired off with\n"
"females.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/14
msgid ""
"The pupils practice their technique for seven years\n"
"before striking out on their own\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/15
msgid ""
"and finding their own pupils.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/16
msgid ""
"I guess it takes time to get good at anything,\n"
"whether it's dancing or soldiering.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/17
msgid ""
"Manakins always have plenty to eat.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/18
msgid ""
"Apparently that is why they have so much free\n"
"time to practice dancing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/19
msgid ""
"Unlike us, obviously...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 445..1852
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/0
msgid ""
"Another well-known bird of the cloud forest is the\n"
"Three-wattled Bellbird.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 1894..2730
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/1
msgid ""
"Wattled? What the hell's a wattle?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 3092..3705
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/2
msgid ""
"It is just like your beard, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 3970..4931
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/4
msgid ""
"It's a piece of flesh that hangs down from its chin.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 4973..5795
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/5
msgid ""
"Kind of like whiskers, but not made of hair.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 5809..6534
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/6
msgid ""
"A hanging piece of flesh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 6561..7370
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/7
msgid ""
"Oui, and it only grows on males.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 7383..8247
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/8
msgid ""
"Nothing more important to a man than his beard.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 8498..9348
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/9
msgid ""
"So these birds are in the cloud forest, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 9418..10281
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/10
msgid ""
"They're normally found in the lowland rain forests,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 10323..11661
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/11
msgid ""
"but they migrate into the highland cloud forests\n"
"during breeding season.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 11744..13068
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/12
msgid ""
"What the Three-wattled Bellbird's best known for,\n"
"though, is its loud call.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 13179..14851
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/13
msgid ""
"It makes these metallic BONG! and DING! sounds -\n"
"hence the name \"bellbird.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 14893..15534
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/14
msgid ""
"It hardly sounds like a bird at all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 15575..16676
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/15
msgid ""
"Even an expert bird caller like me cannot do it\n"
"justice.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 16815..17749
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/16
msgid ""
"Doesn't sound like I'll be mistaking it for a quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 445..1351
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/0
msgid ""
"The Scarlet Macaw and the Great Green Macaw\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 1351..2229
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/1
msgid ""
"are also representative birds of Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 2368..3608
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/2
msgid ""
"Macaws are a type of parrot... enormous, stately\n"
"birds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 3761..4931
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/3
msgid ""
"Macaw... I think I've heard that name somewhere\n"
"before.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 5168..6144
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/4
msgid ""
"But of course you have - you're an ornithologist,\n"
"no?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 6171..6492
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/5
msgid ""
"Stop it....\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 6673..8122
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/6
msgid ""
"So tell me, where do macaws live in Costa Rica\n"
"today?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 8192..8721
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/7
msgid ""
"Oh c'mon now...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 9139..9696
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/8
msgid ""
"I am only teasing you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 9752..10574
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/9
msgid ""
"Macaws live not in the cloud forests,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 10574..11772
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/10
msgid ""
"but in the rain forests on the Pacific side of Costa\n"
"Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 11842..13207
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/11
msgid ""
"In the past, they were a common sight all across\n"
"the country,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 13249..14419
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/12
msgid ""
"but lately the population has decreased\n"
"dramatically.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 14517..16384
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/13
msgid ""
"One possible cause is the pesticides sprayed to\n"
"facilitate large-scale banana cultivation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 16467..17136
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/14
msgid ""
"Evicted from their own land, huh.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 17164..18543
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/15
msgid ""
"Thankfully, conservation efforts have been gaining\n"
"some momentum lately.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/0
msgid ""
"Never heard the name \"Cosima\" before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/1
msgid ""
"The again I don't know many people from France.\n"
"Is it a common name?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/2
msgid ""
"No. Not that common.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/3
msgid ""
"But Wagner's second wife was named Cosima\n"
"Francesca Gaetana Wagner.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 5739..5935
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/4
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/6
msgid ""
"Huh.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/5
msgid ""
"You know, \"Kojima\" is a common last name in Japan.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/7
msgid ""
"It's just funny how, you know,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/8
msgid ""
"I'm part Japanese and Cécile's middle name is so\n"
"close to \"Kojima.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/9
msgid ""
"It feels like... destiny unfolding.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/11
msgid ""
"Oui oui! That's a beautiful name you have. Cécile\n"
"Cosima Caminades.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/12
msgid ""
"Wait a second...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/13
msgid ""
"Cécile Cosima Caminades... Cosima Caminades...\n"
"Hey, that’s close to...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/14
msgid ""
"Close to what?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/15
msgid ""
"Your name... It sounds almost like the sentence\n"
"“Kojima, kaminandesu” in Japanese.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/16
msgid ""
"And what does it mean, s’il vous plait?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/17
msgid ""
"Well, \"kami\" is the word for \"god\" in Japanese.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/18
msgid ""
"\"Nandesu...\" Well, it's hard to explain, but placed\n"
"after \"god\" it would turn the sentence into \"is God.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/19
msgid ""
"Okay. So?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/20
msgid ""
"\"Kojima is God\"... Cecile's name is a message!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/21
msgid ""
"I don’t believe it... Kojima is God... Kojima is God...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/22
msgid ""
"Umm, Kaz...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 445..1253
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/0
msgid ""
"Did you live in Paris your whole life before coming\n"
"here?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 1434..2368
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/1
msgid ""
"Yes. It is my favorite city.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 2549..3566
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/2
msgid ""
"Paris is the world capital of art and culture.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 3664..5489
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/3
msgid ""
"It has the latest fashion, the best cuisine, and the\n"
"most elegant, refined people.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 5614..7147
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/4
msgid ""
"The beauty of the Champs-Élysées at night is\n"
"almost unearthly.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 7230..8554
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/5
msgid ""
"The name comes from Elysium, the name of\n"
"Paradise in Greek mythology.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 8721..9236
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/6
msgid ""
"Heaven, in other words.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 9654..10755
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/7
msgid ""
"Must be nice for some people. Not for me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 10769..11674
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/8
msgid ""
"Are you saying the cultured life does not appeal to\n"
"you?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 11688..13151
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/9
msgid ""
"I'm saying I never had a chance to lead one. Not\n"
"that it appealed to me anyway.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 13165..13583
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/10
msgid ""
"You prefer war?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 13597..15464
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/11
msgid ""
"I don't... Like war. Life outside heaven just suits me\n"
"better.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 15492..16077
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/12
msgid ""
"That is a hard way to live...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 16119..17902
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/13
msgid ""
"...But if you do ever come to France, I will show\n"
"you around Paris.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 18000..19253
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/14
msgid ""
"Then you will see what heaven on earth is really\n"
"like.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 459..1978
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/0
msgid ""
"Heaven on earth, huh... The only image I have of\n"
"France is the Foreign Legion.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/1
msgid ""
"Th-that is how you view France?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/2
msgid ""
"What do the French think of the them?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/3
msgid ""
"It is a difficult question... We normally don't think\n"
"about it so much.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/4
msgid ""
"Critics claim it forces foreigners to take on the\n"
"most dangerous missions\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/5
msgid ""
"so French citizens won't get hurt.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/6
msgid ""
"You're right, that probably had something to do\n"
"with why it was created...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/7
msgid ""
"But I understand that along with service comes\n"
"benefits\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/8
msgid ""
"such as French citizenship and permanent\n"
"residency.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/9
msgid ""
"Those who join are all given an equal chance,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/10
msgid ""
"regardless of race, religion, education, social\n"
"status, or national origin.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/11
msgid ""
"So it can be a godsend for people from poor\n"
"countries.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/12
msgid ""
"A way for the have-nots to live a decent life...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/13
msgid ""
"I guess that's not so different from MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 459..1630
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/0
msgid ""
"There's one other image I have of France: the\n"
"national anthem.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 1643..3260
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/1
msgid ""
"Ah, La Marseillaise... Not everyone is a fan, of\n"
"course.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 3622..5057
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/2
msgid ""
"The whole \"To arms, citizens. May an impure blood\n"
"water our furrows.\" thing, eh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 5071..6283
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/3
msgid ""
"The song was composed right after the French\n"
"Revolution.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 6352..7188
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/4
msgid ""
"Fearing what the tide of the Revolution\n"
"represented,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 7202..7941
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/5
msgid ""
"the ruling classes in neighboring countries applied\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 7941..8791
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/6
msgid ""
"all kinds of pressure on the young government.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 8818..10253
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/7
msgid ""
"La Marseillaise became the anthem of the\n"
"volunteer armies that sought to protect\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 10267..11145
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/8
msgid ""
"constitutional rule against that pressure.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 11159..11911
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/9
msgid ""
"And they couldn't do that without armed force.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 11939..13235
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/10
msgid ""
"Oui. I agree, some parts are a little belligerent,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 13291..14489
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/11
msgid ""
"but we must not forget that if it were not for\n"
"them,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 14558..15589
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/12
msgid ""
"France would not be the democracy it is today.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 445..1239
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/0
msgid ""
"Have you ever seen \"The Umbrellas of Cherbourg\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 1309..2145
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/1
msgid ""
"A movie? No, never seen it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 2173..3120
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/2
msgid ""
"No? It came out 10 years ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 3650..4890
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/3
msgid ""
"Catherine Deneuve, she is so beautiful in it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 5015..6603
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/4
msgid ""
"And the music, the costumes, the colors... Oh!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 6979..8052
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/5
msgid ""
"It takes place in the naval port of Cherbourg.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 8094..8693
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/6
msgid ""
"That was a beachhead in Normandy.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 8735..10100
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/7
msgid ""
"It is set back when young men were conscripted to\n"
"fight in the Algerian War.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 10407..11939
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/8
msgid ""
"The French government called the conflict a\n"
"\"public order operation in northern Africa.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 11995..12552
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/9
msgid ""
"I was still a little girl then,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 12650..14182
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/10
msgid ""
"but I can clearly remember one of my friends' older\n"
"brothers going off to fight.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 14196..15185
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, national service is required in France.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 15213..16021
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/12
msgid ""
"The war splits up two young lovers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 16175..18083
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/13
msgid ""
"Director Jacque Demy's lyrics and Michel Legrand's\n"
"music tore at my heart.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 18250..19435
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/14
msgid ""
"I will never forget its wonderful melodies. Aaahh...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 19518..19894
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/15
msgid ""
"You okay?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 20006..22137
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/16
msgid ""
"It changes lives - changes fates. War is not a good\n"
"thing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 22277..23614
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/17
msgid ""
"For some reason it strikes a chord to hear that\n"
"coming from someone like you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 459..1212
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/0
msgid ""
"Speaking of the Algerian War of Independence,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 1239..1839
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/1
msgid ""
"you ever hear of \"The Day of the Jackal\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 2103..3078
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/2
msgid ""
"You mean the novel that was made into a movie\n"
"last year?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 3120..4207
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/3
msgid ""
"The OAS, a militant French underground group,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 4221..5907
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/4
msgid ""
"plots to assassinate De Gaulle, hiring a hitman\n"
"known as the Jackal.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 5962..7509
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/5
msgid ""
"Readers know that de Gaulle was not killed, but it\n"
"is still so exciting.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 7551..8442
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/6
msgid ""
"If someone was going to try to eliminate me,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 8498..9334
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/7
msgid ""
"I would hope they'd be as thorough as the Jackal.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 9404..10685
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/8
msgid ""
"To know everything about me without me\n"
"suspecting a thing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 10727..11006
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/9
msgid ""
"Oh, Yeah?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/10
msgid ""
"I wonder if my birds feel the same way.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/11
msgid ""
"I wonder.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 473..2215
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/0
msgid ""
"France conducted its first successful nuclear test\n"
"in the Algerian Sahara in 1960.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 2340..3246
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/1
msgid ""
"A lot of French scientists took part in the\n"
"Manhattan Project.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 3343..4346
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/2
msgid ""
"They defected to America to escape wartime\n"
"occupation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 4416..5126
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/3
msgid ""
"Correct. And once the war was over,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 5154..6394
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/4
msgid ""
"they returned to France and continued their own\n"
"atomic research.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 6408..8317
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/5
msgid ""
"President de Gaulle did not want to have to rely\n"
"on an American nuclear umbrella for protection.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 8359..9404
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/6
msgid ""
"Thus making France the world's fourth nuclear\n"
"power.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 9431..10699
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/7
msgid ""
"Some say the test's success pacified the Algerian\n"
"rebels.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 10769..11577
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/8
msgid ""
"The civil war was undoubtedly held in check.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 11633..13054
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/9
msgid ""
"But never have I equated nuclear weapons with\n"
"peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/0
msgid ""
"France has produced many philosophers over the\n"
"years.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/1
msgid ""
"Descartes, Bataille, Sartre, Baudrillard...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/2
msgid ""
"I'm familiar with Sartre myself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/3
msgid ""
"He called Che Guevara the most complete man of\n"
"the century, didn't he?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/4
msgid ""
"Smart guy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/5
msgid ""
"He does tend to sympathize with the left. What\n"
"else do you know about him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/6
msgid ""
"...That's it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/7
msgid ""
"You know nothing else?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/8
msgid ""
"...Nope.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/9
msgid ""
"Ooh la la. The man is one of the giants of\n"
"existentialism, you know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/10
msgid ""
"Exitentialism? I've been meaning to look into that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/11
msgid ""
"Nothing more dangerous than sneaking in without\n"
"first securing an exit...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/12
msgid ""
"No, existentialism. Sometimes I wonder if my\n"
"English is not better than yours.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/13
msgid ""
"Sorry, I'm just... not into philosophy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/14
msgid ""
"Is that so? I would imagine it might really enrich\n"
"your life.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/15
msgid ""
"I'd rather take action now than spend time thinking\n"
"about\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/16
msgid ""
"what we are or how we're supposed to live.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/17
msgid ""
"I guess you could say I live my philosophy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/18
msgid ""
"Interesting. That sounds like something Sartre\n"
"would say.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/20
msgid ""
"He says we're born with no defined nature,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/21
msgid ""
"and that we're free to make our \"self\" what we wish.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/22
msgid ""
"Free? So he was one of those devil-may-care kind\n"
"of guys, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/23
msgid ""
"No, actually he meant that because we are free to\n"
"create our own life,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/24
msgid ""
"we must take full responsibility for our actions.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/25
msgid ""
"\"Man is condemned to be free,\" is how he put it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/26
msgid ""
"Condemned to be free...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/27
msgid ""
"But then others will take it upon themselves to\n"
"define who you are.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/28
msgid ""
"I've been feeling that way lately.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/29
msgid ""
"I keep telling people to call me \"Snake,\" but nobody\n"
"seems to listen.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/30
msgid ""
"Sartre also says, \"Hell is other people.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/31
msgid ""
"Hell... Well we are outside of Heaven.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/0
msgid ""
"Tell me, Snake, do you ever put sweets in your\n"
"rations?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/1
msgid ""
"Never thought about it before. Why?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/2
msgid ""
"I simply love them! French sweets are très délicieux.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/3
msgid ""
"Everyone knows crêpes, but there are also\n"
"profiteroles,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/4
msgid ""
"éclairs, madeleines, financiers...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/5
msgid ""
"Then there's Tarte Tatins, and you can't forget\n"
"savarins.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/6
msgid ""
"Oh, and mille-feuilles, crêpes, blancmanges...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/7
msgid ""
"You already mentioned crêpes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/8
msgid ""
"Soufflés, croquembouches, canelés, floretins, kouign\n"
"amanns, Peach Melbas...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/9
msgid ""
"Finished?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/10
msgid ""
"...And macarons! I love those the most.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/11
msgid ""
"Macarons parisiens are the best.They're so cute\n"
"and colorful,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/12
msgid ""
"and they contain meringue, so they melt right in\n"
"your mouth.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/13
msgid ""
"Wow. I'd no idea macaroons were that popular in\n"
"France, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/14
msgid ""
"What do you mean \"in France, too\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/15
msgid ""
"Macaroons are those coconut-flavored cookies,\n"
"right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/16
msgid ""
"Excuse you! Macarons contains almond powder, not\n"
"coconuts!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/17
msgid ""
"Don't they have peanuts in them? I've had them in\n"
"Japan a few times.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/18
msgid ""
"I thought they were called \"makorons.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/19
msgid ""
"Makarons? Some cheap imitation, I am sure.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/20
msgid ""
"French macarons have a long and distinguished\n"
"history.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/21
msgid ""
"They date back to the 16th century, when\n"
"Catherine de' Medici of Florence\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/22
msgid ""
"married into the French royal family.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/23
msgid ""
"The story goes that her pâtissiers shared the\n"
"recipe after they arrived.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/24
msgid ""
"That's a history of over 500 years.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/25
msgid ""
"So... they're originally from Italy, then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/26
msgid ""
"Well...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/27
msgid ""
"Don't macaroons come from Italy, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/28
msgid ""
"Look, I do not really think...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/29
msgid ""
"Keep in mind \"macaron\" is almost identical to\n"
"\"macaroni.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/30
msgid ""
"Well, that settles it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/31
msgid ""
"...I cannot believe this. To associate macarons with\n"
"macaroni!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/32
msgid ""
"You, Monsieur Miller, are an insensible oaf!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/33
msgid ""
"Hey, hey, why am I the bad guy? Come on, Cécile,\n"
"wait! Cécile!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/0
msgid ""
"Hello! Snake, mon chéri.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/1
msgid ""
"You been drinking, Cécile?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/2
msgid ""
"Can't you please do something about this pest?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/3
msgid ""
"Who?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/4
msgid ""
"Monsieur Miller.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/5
msgid ""
"What's he done now...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/6
msgid ""
"Wine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/7
msgid ""
"Wine?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/8
msgid ""
"He said he thought the soldiers might tire of\n"
"having beer all the time,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/9
msgid ""
"so he's brought in some wine instead. And then he\n"
"gave me a bunch.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/10
msgid ""
"That was... nice of him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/11
msgid ""
"But the past two years have been bad for French\n"
"wine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/12
msgid ""
"Perhaps it is the bad weather we have had, but\n"
"whatever the case,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/13
msgid ""
"I told him the last thing you want to be drinking\n"
"right now is French wine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/14
msgid ""
"California and Chile have good wine, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/15
msgid ""
"But then he goes and stocks the pantry with\n"
"nothing but French wine from '72.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/16
msgid ""
"The stuff is a disaster.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/17
msgid ""
"Then he says, \"Come on, Cécile, have a taste of\n"
"the old country.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/18
msgid ""
"I had a terrible feeling about it, so I decided to just\n"
"taste it at first.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/19
msgid ""
"And then again, and then a few more times.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/20
msgid ""
"Took one for the team, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/21
msgid ""
"But when you do a tasting, don't you usually spit\n"
"the wine out?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/22
msgid ""
"But bottle after bottle, nothing but garbage,\n"
"absolute garbage.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/23
msgid ""
"Not one half-decent bottle in the whole lot! \"Taste\n"
"of the old country\" he says...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/24
msgid ""
"Sorry to hear that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/25
msgid ""
"I cannot believe this! What will we do with all this\n"
"wine!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/26
msgid ""
"The guys aren't too picky when it comes to taste.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/27
msgid ""
"You sound just like Monsieur Miller.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/29
msgid ""
"When I complained, he simply said, \"As long as it\n"
"gets the job done.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/30
msgid ""
"You people are such culinary savages!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/31
msgid ""
"Allez tous vous faire voir ! ...Aaaah, somebody take\n"
"me back to Paris! Please!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/32
msgid ""
"...I think you've had a little too much, Cécile.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 459..2020
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/0
msgid ""
"Doc, I'm starting to sense your feelings about\n"
"nukes are a little different from your colleagues.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 2340..3009
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/2
msgid ""
"Your little chat with Coldman back there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 3023..4472
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/3
msgid ""
"I...told you my father worked on the Manhattan\n"
"Project, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 4625..5015
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/4
msgid ""
"You're familiar with it?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 5085..6213
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/5
msgid ""
"The basics, yeah. It was the project that kicked off\n"
"the nuclear age.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 6227..7300
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/6
msgid ""
"That's right. Some of the finest minds of the 20th\n"
"century,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 7300..8317
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/7
msgid ""
"including multiple Nobel Prize winners, worked on it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 8359..9808
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/8
msgid ""
"They spent over two billion dollars - and that's in\n"
"1940's money.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 9822..11605
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/9
msgid ""
"It culminated in the successful nuclear test at\n"
"Alamogordo on July 16, 1945.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 11605..12566
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/10
msgid ""
"And the first use in combat a few weeks later.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 12873..13082
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/11
msgid ""
"Doc?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 13096..13444
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/12
msgid ""
"...I can't walk.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 13597..15074
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/13
msgid ""
"My spine isn't shaped like everybody else's. I can't\n"
"move my lower body.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 15088..16063
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/14
msgid ""
"So I've never taken a single step, not since I was\n"
"born.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 16077..16983
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/15
msgid ""
"What's that got to do with your dad being in the\n"
"Manhattan Project?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 16983..18543
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/16
msgid ""
"As a result of his research, my father was exposed\n"
"to high doses of radiation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 18640..19658
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/17
msgid ""
"It can't be a coincidence that my chromosomes are\n"
"messed up.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 19964..20243
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/18
msgid ""
"That's...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 20271..21524
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/19
msgid ""
"That's why I didn't want for these nukes to be\n"
"another sword of Damocles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 21538..22764
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/20
msgid ""
"I wanted to give them a real purpose: to be a\n"
"deterrent against war.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 22778..22987
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/21
msgid ""
"Doc...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 23001..24520
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/22
msgid ""
"And Coldman... We have to stop him. Whatever it\n"
"takes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 445..1546
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/0
msgid ""
"It wasn't so long ago the world stood on the brink\n"
"of nuclear war.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 1546..2187
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/1
msgid ""
"Just over on the other side of the Caribbean.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 2201..3873
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/2
msgid ""
"I was 17 at the time. I'd skipped a few grades and\n"
"was a sophomore at MIT.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 4026..5126
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/3
msgid ""
"I remember feeling kind of apathetic about the\n"
"news that came in every day.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 5182..6617
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/4
msgid ""
"It seemed clear to me that as long as they had a\n"
"grasp of the concept of nuclear deterrence,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 6617..7119
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/5
msgid ""
"there was nothing to fear.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 7272..8400
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/6
msgid ""
"Either that, or they were fanning that fear on\n"
"purpose.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 8400..9947
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/7
msgid ""
"As a way to secure a bigger defense budget...?\n"
"Heh, I can see that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 9961..10727
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/8
msgid ""
"But if that was their plan, it kind of backfired.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 10741..11856
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/9
msgid ""
"Because it ushered in the era of Détente between\n"
"East and West.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 11856..12678
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/10
msgid ""
"Coldman's really going to do it this time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 12747..13346
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/11
msgid ""
"Once the nuclear genie is out of the bottle,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 13346..14182
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/12
msgid ""
"the yoke of deterrence is going to be meaningless.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 14196..15116
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/13
msgid ""
"People will die. Cities will burn.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 15116..16161
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/14
msgid ""
"We have to stop him now, before it's too late to\n"
"turn back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/0
msgid ""
"But you know... there's something I've never been\n"
"able to figure out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/1
msgid ""
"Is the Cold War really a war, or is it really peace...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/2
msgid ""
"Doc, what are you...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/3
msgid ""
"People called it a \"cold war,\" but I disagreed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/4
msgid ""
"Sure, nuclear stockpiles are increasing, threats are\n"
"multiplying,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/5
msgid ""
"the U.S. and the Soviet Union have enough power\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/6
msgid ""
"to destroy the human race a hundred times over.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/7
msgid ""
"But nobody's actually being killed. Small-scale\n"
"conflicts and proxy wars, maybe...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/8
msgid ""
"But nuclear deterrence has averted another world\n"
"war.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/9
msgid ""
"The world's far more peaceful today than it was\n"
"before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/10
msgid ""
"And the breakthroughs we've made in space\n"
"exploration\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/11
msgid ""
"thanks to Cold War competition - fantastic, don't\n"
"you think?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/12
msgid ""
"No... We didn't need to rush into space like that...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/13
msgid ""
"Going into space may have been mankind's dream,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/14
msgid ""
"but good people were sacrificed in the scramble.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/15
msgid ""
"...Maybe so. NASA's definitely got some skeletons in\n"
"its closet...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/16
msgid ""
"Same goes for the nuclear arms race.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/17
msgid ""
"Atomic testing has killed civilians and exposed\n"
"thousands to radiation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/18
msgid ""
"Believe me, I know...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/19
msgid ""
"And now this... What peace was I trying to protect,\n"
"anyway?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/20
msgid ""
"The more I think about it, the less I understand.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 445..1421
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/0
msgid ""
"Nuclear deterrence means preventing the use of\n"
"nuclear weapons\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 1421..2661
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/1
msgid ""
"in conflicts between states. But what about other\n"
"situations?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 2953..3761
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/3
msgid ""
"Terrorism has been on the rise in recent years,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 3761..4736
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/4
msgid ""
"from separatist movements to far-left extremists.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 4736..6018
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/5
msgid ""
"What would happen if nuclear weapons fell into\n"
"terrorist hands?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 6018..7091
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/6
msgid ""
"Without a state - that is, without territory of their\n"
"own\n"
msgstr ""
